@* The announcement that AKML SQL now supports SQL Server Management Studio 22 only. One component
   so the home and download pages say exactly the same thing. It must stay true to the installer:
   setup offers SSMS 22 as the only host and, on an upgrade, deletes the Extensions\AkmlSql folder
   earlier releases put into Visual Studio 2026 (RemoveLegacyVSExtensions in AkmlSqlSetup.iss). *@
<aside class="notice host-notice" aria-labelledby="@HeadingId">
    <h2 id="@HeadingId">Now for SQL Server Management Studio 22 only</h2>
    <p>
        The AKML SQL extension works in SQL Server Management Studio 22. Visual Studio 2026 is no
        longer supported: setup installs into SSMS 22 only, and when you upgrade it removes the
        extension earlier versions added to Visual Studio.
    </p>
</aside>

@code {
    /// <summary>Unique per page, so the heading id never collides with the page's own.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string HeadingId { get; set; } = "host-support-heading";
}
